dEBLCPdN$TdCStdUtOrBLW  aMAIN 4aQC665.E4 7aTHR2bicssc 7aTEC0070002bisacsh 7aTHR2thema04a530.14/1223/eng/202408261 aAlkhoori, Hamad M.,eauthor.10aConcise introduction to electromagnetic fields /cHamad M. Alkhoori 1aCham :bSpringer,c2025  a1 online resource (xii, 277 pages) :billustrations (some color)  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aSynthesis lectures on electromagnetics,x2691-54560 aIntroduction to Electromagnetics and Essential Mathematics -- Maxwell equations and the structure of electromagnetics -- Vector algebra and vector calculus -- Time Independent Electromagnetics -- Electrostatics -- Currents and resistance -- Magnetostatics -- Time Dependent Electromagnetics -- Quasi statics and dynamics -- Plane wave propagation -- Plane wave reflection and refraction -- Transmission lines -- Waveguides and cavities -- Radiation and Antennas -- Antenna fundamentals -- Electromagnetic radiation and auxiliary potentials -- Wire antennas -- Antenna arrays -- Integral equations  aThis book introduces electrical engineering students and practitioners to the subject of electromagnetics. The book begins with a review of essential mathematical topics and then shifts to the topics of electrostatics, magnetostatics, time-varying electromagnetics, and antennas. Coverage includes a wide range of topics in electromagnetics with clear and simple descriptions of necessary concepts and worked-out examples, as well as explanations of relevant physics. The book can serve as a primary reference for undergraduate-level electromagnetics courses and a quick review of elementary pre-requisite topics in graduate-level electromagnetics courses  aIncludes bibliographical references0 aOnline resource; title from PDF title page (SpringerLink, viewed August 26, 2024) 0aElectromagnetic fields.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85042168 6aChamps électromagnétiques. 7aelectromagnetism.2a