-- Chains (3:25) -- In spring (3:10) -- Tokens (2:52) -- Again (2:58) -- Next time around (4:26) -- Only fools (3:58) -- Reminder (2:51) 0aPiano music.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85101782 6aPiano, Musique de.0(CaQQLa)201-000826002iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tOnce a dream.02iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tOnly fools.02iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tChains.02iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tIn spring.02iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tTokens.02iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tAgain.02iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tNext time around.02iContainer of (work):aSequoiac(Musician).tReminder.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttp://stanford.naxosmusiclibrary.com/catalogue/item.asp?cid=PM00916yNaxos Music LibraryxProvider: NaxosxCollection: Naxos Music LibraryxsubscribedxeLoaderURLxnm4xnmon1452123146  aeLoaderRecord xnm4ffi0027a694-5016-4c1b-9830-8ea3017067ads87ddbd3f-2c03-44ac-acd5-82baa90090a703669cam a2200517 i in0000018466820250403134755.0m     o  d        cr un|---aucuu240106s2024    si      ob    000 0 eng d  a1430324033a1443088429  a9789819979066q(electronic bk.)  a9819979064q(electronic bk.)  z9819979056  z97898199790597 a10.1007/978-981-99-7906-62doi  aspon1416725177  a(OCoLC-M)1416725177z(OCoLC)1430324033z(OCoLC)1443088429  aYDXbengcYDXdOCLCOdGW5XEdOCLCOdEBLCPdN$TdOCLCQdQGKdUKAHLdCStdUtOrBLW  aMAIN 4aTA705 7aTNC2bicssc 7aSCI0420002bisacsh 7aTNC2thema04a624.1/51223/eng/202401181 aRoy, Mihir.10aGeotechnical and foundation engineering practice in industrial projectsh[electronic resource] /cMihir Roy  aSingapore :bSpringer,c2024  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aChapter 1. Introduction to Chapters -- Chapter 2. Engineering Geology -- Chapter 3. Geotechnical Investigation -- Chapter 4. Site Development -- Chapter 5. Ground Improvement -- Chapter 6. Foundation on Soft & Filled-up Soil -- Chapter 7. Pile Foundation -- Chapter 8. Seepage Control -- Chapter 9. Erosion Control & Retaining Wall -- Chapter 10. Marine Projects -- Chapter 11. Simplified Liquefaction Potential Assessment -- Chapter 12. Tailing Storage Management at Mines -- Chapter 13. Failure During Construction -- Chapter 14. Site Hazard & Remedy -- Chapter 15. Practice in Geotechnical & Foundation Engineering -- Appendices  aThis professional book is an important resource on the topics of geotechnical and foundation engineering for practicing engineers and consultants. It fills the gap between classroom education and real-world professional practice in green and brown field projects. It provides hands-on knowledge on various topics such as engineering geology, geotechnical investigation, site preparation, ground improvement, foundation on soft and filled-up soil, pile foundation, seepage control, erosion control and retaining wall, marine projects, simplified liquefaction potential assessment, tailing storage management at mines, failure during construction, site hazard and remedy and geotechnical and foundation engineering practice. This book will be highly useful for professionals and practicing engineers in the area of geotechnical and foundations engineering. It will also be a useful reference for graduate and postgraduate students and the faculty in the same field  aIncludes bibliographical references0 aOnline resource; title from PDF title page (SpringerLink, viewed January 18, 2024) 0aGeotechnical engineering.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2013000289 0aFoundations.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85051049 6aGéologie appliquée. 6aFondations (Construction) 7afoundations (structural elements)2aat08iPrint version:z9819979056z9789819979059w(OCoLC)140220123840zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://link.springer.com