btxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aThe author's experiences as a submarine commander in the British Royal Navy during World War II0 aBefore -- Snapper -- Trusty -- In between -- Telemachus -- After  aSAL3 copy: Walter L. Leschander collection, 1938-1965d36105212332204 0aWorld War, 1939-1945zGreat BritainxNaval operations. 0aWorld War, 1939-1945xNaval operationsxSubmarine.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85148451 6aGuerre mondiale, 1939-1945xOpérations sous-marines. 7aMilitary operations, NavalxSubmarine.2fast0(OCoLC)fst017102480http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1710248 7aWorld Ward(1939-1945)2fast0(OCoLC)fst011809240http://id.worldcat.org/fast/11809241https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39Qhp4vBbhpRH9XvjbDFXtxhb 7a1939-19452fast 7aPersonal narratives.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026142  ihas work:aThe stick and the stars (Text)1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCGvxkyVxHx9xJwc7WXKyBP4https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/ontology/hasWork08iOnline version:aKing, W. D. Æ. (William Donald Ælian), 1910-2012.tStick and the stars.b[1st ed.]dNew York, Norton, [1958]w(OCoLC)1103440342  aWalter L. Leschander collection, 1938-1965423Related manuscript collectionuhttps://searchworks.stanford.edu/view/4088204  aZ0bSTF  hHELD BY STF - 84 OTHER HOLDINGSffs5cb5e0dd-7a3b-423a-8bc4-d101980aa73ei0028616e-1aca-4293-9264-f521511401f704583cam a2200529 i in0000018739920250403134755.0m     o  d        cr un|---aucuu240701s2024    sz a    ob    001 0 eng d  a1440669349a1441722021  a9783031601033q(electronic bk.)  a3031601033q(electronic bk.)  z9783031601026  z30316010257 a10.1007/978-3-031-60103-32doi  aspon1443164874  a(OCoLC-M)1443164874z(OCoLC)1440669349z(OCoLC)1441722021  aGW5XEbengerdaepncGW5XEdOCLCOdYDXdEBLCPdOCLCQdCStdUtOrBLW  aMAIN 4aQA402.5 7aUYQ2bicssc 7aCOM0040002bisacsh 7aUYQ2thema04a519.6/4223/eng/202407011 aBlum, Christian,d1972-eauthor.1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjxdh7rch8rRhRykrGy68C0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n200804999010aConstruct, merge, solve & adapt :ba hybrid metaheuristic for combinatorial optimization /cChristian Blum 1aCham :bSpringer,c2024  a1 online resource (xvi, 192 pages) :billustrations (some color)  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aComputational intelligence methods and applications,x2510-17730 aIntroduction to CMSA -- Self-Adaptive CMSA -- Adding Learning to CMSA -- Replacing Hard Mathematical Models with Set Covering Formulations -- Application of CMSA in the Presence of Non-Binary Variables -- Additional Research Lines Concerning CMSA  aThis book describes a general hybrid metaheuristic for combinatorial optimization labeled Construct, Merge, Solve & Adapt (CMSA). The general idea of standard CMSA is the following one. At each iteration, a number of valid solutions to the tackled problem instance are generated in a probabilistic way. Hereby, each of these solutions is composed of a set of solution components. The components found in the generated solutions are then added to an initially empty sub-instance. Next, an exact solver is applied in order to compute the best solution of the sub-instance, which is then used to update the sub-instance provided as input for the next iteration. In this way, the power of exact solvers can be exploited for solving problem instances much too large for a standalone application of the solver. Important research lines on CMSA from recent years are covered in this book. After an introductory chapter about standard CMSA, subsequent chapters cover a self-adaptive CMSA variant as well as a variant equipped with a learning component for improving the quality of the generated solutions over time. Furthermore, on outlining the advantages of using set-covering-based integer linear programming models for sub-instance solving, the author shows how to apply CMSA to problems naturally modelled by non-binary integer linear programming models. The book concludes with a chapter on topics such as the development of a problem-agnostic CMSA and the relation between large neighborhood search and CMSA. Combinatorial optimization problems used in the book as test cases include the minimum dominating set problem, the variable-sized bin packing problem, and an electric vehicle routing problem. The book will be valuable and is intended for researchers, professionals and graduate students working in a wide range of fields, such as combinatorial optimization, algorithmics, metaheuristics, mathematical modeling, evolutionary computing, operations research, artificial intelligence, or statistics  aIncludes bibliographical references and index0 aOnline resource; title from PDF title page (SpringerLink, viewed July 1, 2024) 0aCombinatorial optimization.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85028809 0aMetaheuristics.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2016000809 6aOptimisation combinatoire. 6aMétaheuristiques.08cOriginalz3031601025z9783031601026w(OCoLC)1429281994 0aComputational Intelligence Methods and Applications.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://link.springer.com/10.1007/978-3-031-60103-3xWMSySpringerLinkxProvider: SpringerxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxsp4xspon1443164874  aeLoaderRecord xsp4  a92bSTFffi002881e0-a600-426e-b272-336dea948557s6edc4d0e-4cf3-4611-abfd-77cec19f89fa02445nim a2200433ui in0000030088520250403134755.0i||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu191117s2018||||xx ||||go||||||z  | eng|d  als23379  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aHidden Noise Episode 13 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bEven Magazine,c2018  a1 online resource  aspoken wordbspw2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aHidden Noise ;v13  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"On episode 13 of Hidden Noise, hosts Abby Sandler and Rebecca Siegel visit the Met Breuer for this week's Go See: "Like Life: Sculpture, Color, and the Body (1300-now)." Then the hosts are joined by Peter Russo, director of Triple Canopy for the Even 8."--cprovided by distributor  aStandard Copyright10aArt--Exhibitions.10aArtxHistory.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500748810aSculpture.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8511900417aArt History.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0081539617aExhibitions.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008152390http://id.worldcat.org/fast/91809717aSculpture.2fast0(OCoLC)fst011094830http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1109483 7aPodcasts.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2011026450 7aPodcasts.2fast0(OCoLC)fst017502150http://id.worldcat.org/fast/17502151 aRusso, Peter,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20190097091 aSandler, Abby,eeditor.1 aSiegel, Rebecca Ann,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20181713472 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://www.librarystack.org/hidden-noise-episode-13/yLibrary StackxProvider: Library StackxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxls4zTo create lists or check out books that are not open access, users must create a Library Stack account.xls2337942uhttps://www.librarystack.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Hidden-Noise-Logo-2-240x240.jpgzCover Image Preview  aeLoaderRecord xls4ffi002952ca-d1f4-466e-9305-15eee3f0a299sd072afc5-06db-4ed2-8a90-139b24533e5203912cam a22005057i in0000029115120250403134755.0m     o  d        cr un|---|ucuu241130s2024    si      o     100 0 eng d  a1472957593  a9789819764655q(electronic bk.)  a9819764653q(electronic bk.)  z9819764645  z97898197646487 a10.1007/978-981-97-6465-52doi  aspon1474243446  a(OCoLC)1474243446z(OCoLC)1472957593  aEBLCPbengcEBLCPdGW5XEdYDXdEBLCPdOCLCOdYDXdOCLCQdCStdUtOrBLW  aMAIN 4aTK5105.5b.I23 202404a004.6223/eng/202412052 aICCDN (Conference)n(7th :d2024 :cSikkim, India)10aAdvances in Communication, Devices and Networking :bProceedings of ICCDN 2024.nVolume 1 /cSourav Dhar, Subhas Mukhopadhyay, Dinh-Thuan Do, Samarendra Nath Sur, Agbotiname Lucky Imoize, editors3 aICCDN 2024  aSingapore :bSpringer,c2024  a1 online resource (536 p.).1 aLecture Notes in Electrical Engineering ;vv. 12430 a1. High Speed Congestion Aware Routing Algorithm for Network on Chip Architecture -- 2. Impact of Technology Node on Low Power Analog Performance of AU TFET -- 3. Comparative Analysis of the Electrical and Dielectric Characteristics of a Novel Glassy Ceramic and Its Crystalline Analogue -- 4. DFT Investigation of Fe Doped ZnO Monolayer for Adsorption of Toxic Gases -- 5. Printed Circuit Board Assembly Welding Process Based on Computer Aided Design -- 6. Enhancing Endangered Animal Conservation through Deep Learning-Powered Monitoring -- 7. Direct Approach for Modelling a Class of Fractional Order System Using Two Generating Functions -- 8. Classification of Parkinsons and Control Subjects with Machine Learning  aThis book covers recent trends in the field of devices, wireless communication and networking. It gathers selected papers presented at the 7th International Conference on Communication, Devices and Networking (ICCDN 2024), which was organized by the Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Sikkim Manipal Institute of Technology, Sikkim, India, on January 1920, 2024. Gathering cutting-edge research papers prepared by researchers, engineers and industry professionals, it helps young and experienced scientists and developers alike to explore new perspectives and offers them inspirations on how to address real-world problems in the areas of electronics, communication, devices and networking0 aOnline resource; title from PDF title page (SpringerLink, viewed December 5, 2024) 0aComputer networksvCongresses.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008101222 0aWireless communication systemsvCongresses.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008113541 6aTransmission sans filvCongrès.1 aDhar, Sourav.1 aMukhopadhyay, Subhas.1 aĐỗ, Đình Thuận.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20100208671 aSur, Samarendra Nath.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20230080181 aImoize, Agbotiname Lucky.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no202300852508iPrint version:aDhar, SouravtAdvances in Communication, Devices and NetworkingdSingapore : Springer,c2024z9789819764648 0aLecture notes in electrical engineering ;vv. 1234.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200709970940zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps://link.springer.com/10.1007/978-981-97-6465-5xWMSySpringerLinkxProvider: SpringerxpurchasedxeLoaderURLxsp4xspon1474243446  aeLoaderRecord xsp4  a92bSTFffi002e23fa-91fb-47c1-98b1-407d6dbce96esbd895acc-aaf0-44e3-9430-039f4286a4bf01802cam a2200385Mi a630552820250403134755.0071217s2005    tu            000 0 tur d  a9756463619q(pbk.)  a9789756463611  a(OCoLC)on1030087075  a(OCoLC-M)1030087075  aT9KbengcT9KdOCLCOdOCLCFdOCLCQdOCLdOCLCOdOCLCLdHULdOCLCOdUtOrBLW14aPL243.M36bA88 20051 aManisalı, Erol.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no880005591https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJvXjfG4CVkMkVd7Jck7HC10aAttila İlhan'la akıp giden düşünceler /cErol Manisalı  aİstanbul :bDerin,c2005  a165 pages ;c21 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier0 aDerin Yayınları ;v72 0aTurkish essays.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh98000722 0aAuthors, TurkishvBiography.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2009116369 6aÉcrivains turcsvBiographies. 7aAuthors, Turkish.2fast0http://id.worldcat.org/fast/822406 7aTurkish essays.2fast0http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1159405 7aBiographies.2fast0http://id.worldcat.org/fast/19198961 aİlhan, Attilâ,d1925-2005.  ihas work:aAttilâ İlhan'la akıp giden düşünceler (Text)1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCXWgwRj337d33GHXGGK7xP4https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/ontology/hasWork  aMONORECUnit/11 November 2022/jks/CATMARCUnit/Turkish  a6305528  hHELD BY STF - 2 OTHER HOLDINGS  aZ0bSTFffi002fc177-8141-5a94-a476-3a58f6ce9e4fsc37fc5a0-e532-52ab-a3f4-13103e46391a03804cam a2200409 i in0000018035020250403134755.0240408t20242024ilu      b    001 0 eng    a  2024015758  a9781639055074q(paperback)  a163905507Xq(paperback)  z9781639055081q(epub)  a(OCoLC)on1429287030  a(OCoLC-M)1429287030  aDLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdBDXdYDXdPQDdWLLdOCLCOdCLUdGWLdRCJdUtOrBLW  an-us---00aKF298b.P65 202400a658.4/09208834223/eng/202404091 aPolden, Donald J.,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n980199361https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjMkp8j7F48fCjfd6XGbkC10aLawyers as leaders :bwhy it matters and what it takes /cDonald J. Polden and Barry Z. Posner 1aChicago, Illinois :bAmerican Bar Association, Law Practice Division,c[2024] 4c©2024  ax, 230 pages ;c23 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index00gIntroduction --tFoundations of educating lawyers for leadership : why leadership development is essential for lawyers --tLeadership : what it means and why it's important to lawyers --tLawyer-leaders model the way --tLawyer-leaders inspire a shared vision --tLawyer-leaders challenge the process --tLawyer-leaders enable others to act --tLawyer-leaders encourage the heart --tPersonal values and professional ethics as lawyer-leaders --tMaking decisions, leading innovation --tBecoming a team leader --tDeveloping emotional intelligence and handling adversity --tLeading the charge for diversity, equity, and inclusion --gAfterword:tLooking to the future : leadership development to produce better lawyers..  a"This book has two parts. The first part begins by addressing why leadership development and training are essential in preparing lawyers for the roles and responsibilities they will have in their careers. The following six chapters describe The Five Practices of Exemplary Leadership®, providing qualitative and quantitative evidence of how these leadership practices improve personal and organizational productivity and stature. This operational system for leadership forms an accessible and practical basis for learning to lead and becoming the best leader you can be. The five chapters in the second part address the context in which lawyers exercise leadership. For example, thinking about leading in client relationships, in internal relationships (such as within the law firm or corporate legal office), and public roles. Examined are vital issues regarding client development ethics, effective decision-making, building emotional intelligence, diversity, equity and inclusion, and handling conflicts and adversity. In the Afterword, we focus on developing and adopting a leadership development mindset necessary for leading in challenging times. We also offer perspectives on how to be a lawyer leader who positively impacts the legal profession and the world"--cProvided by the publisher 0aLawyerszUnited States.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh87000876 0aLawyerszUnited StatesxPsychology. 0aLeadershipxStudy and teachingzUnited States. 0aPractice of lawxStudy and teachingzUnited States.1 aPosner, Barry Z.,eauthor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n820732571https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJmtvBYFMqrMxQ7VmwG8md  aZ0bRCJ  hNO HOLDINGS IN RCJ - 27 OTHER HOLDINGSffs54801aa1-ad4e-4421-82f2-406c1147a6c3i0031b6c2-d280-4dae-9d12-02cfc61f599903101cas a2200625 i in0000020403520250403134755.0m     o  d        cr cn|||||||||041027c20049999enkqx pso     0   a0eng c  a  2004262350  aGBA6030872bnb7 a0133525332Uk  a1740-9306l1740-9292y1026-0218  a(OCoLC-M)56827996  a(SFX)111087394189000  amr111087394189000  aCGUbengepncCGUdOCLdOCLCQdMUQdOCLdOCLCQdUKMGBdOCLCQdOCLCFdOCLCQdNOCdWT2dNLEdDLCdU3WdOCLCQdAU@dCUSdOCLCQdLDPdCUIdOCLCOdOCLCQdUtOrBLW0 aengafre  apcc  ae-fr---00aPQ104a944.08 0aContemporary French and francophone studiesb(Online)00aContemporary French and francophone studies  a[Oxfordshire, UK] :bTaylor & Francis,c2004-  a1 online resource  aFive issues a year,b2009-  aQuarterly,b2004-2008  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aVol. 8, issue 1 (2004)-  aTitle from table of contents screen (MetaPress website, viewed on Oct. 27, 2004)  aSome issues combined  aArticles in English and French1 aVol. 21, issue 5 (2017) (Taylor & Francis Online, viewed Mar. 15, 2018)0 aMARCit full record. 0aCulturexStudy and teachingzFrancevPeriodicals. 0aFrench literaturevPeriodicals.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh2008121262 6aCulturexÉtude et enseignementzFrancevPériodiques. 6aLittérature françaisevPériodiques. 7aCivilization.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008628980http://id.worldcat.org/fast/862898 7aCulturexStudy and teaching.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008850860http://id.worldcat.org/fast/885086 7aFrench literature.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009346880http://id.worldcat.org/fast/934688 7aFrench Studies.2ebps 0aFrancexCivilizationvPeriodicals. 6aFrancexCivilisationvPériodiques. 7aFrance.2fast0(OCoLC)fst012042890http://id.worldcat.org/fast/1204289 7aPeriodicals.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014116410http://id.worldcat.org/fast/141164108iPrint version:tContemporary French and francophone studiesx1740-9292w(DLC)  2004234080w(OCoLC)5469754700tSites (Amsterdam, Netherlands : Online)w(DLC)  2016236686w(OCoLC)50447051  aeLoaderRecordxmr440uhttp://library.stanford.edu/sfx?url%5Fver=Z39.88-2004&ctx%5Fver=Z39.88-2004&ctx%5Fenc=info:ofi/enc:UTF-8&rfr%5Fid=info:sid/sfxit.com:opac%5F856&url%5Fctx%5Ffmt=info:ofi/fmt:kev:mtx:ctx&sfx.ignore%5Fdate%5Fthreshold=1&rft.object%5Fid=111087394189000&svc%5Fval%5Ffmt=info:ofi/fmt:kev:mtx:sch%5Fsvc&xeLoaderURLxmr4xmr111087394189000ffs21338af8-3190-4fea-acb1-780c59e32d78i00325b34-e6bc-4b28-bce5-831ff0b6b58704921nam a2200793ui in0000030428020250403134755.0a||||go|||||||||||cr mn|---uuuuu210920s2016||||xx ||||go|||||||| u|eng|d  als67629  aNYHLSbengerdacNYHLSdCstdUtOrBLW00aArchifutures Volume 3: The Site 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bdpr-barcelona,c2016 1a[Place of publication not identified] :bFuture Architecture Platform,c2016  a1 online resource  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aArchifutures ;v3  aArchived and cataloged by Library Stack  aUnrestricted online access  a"This volume is a call to practical action leading on from the theoretical approaches seen in Volume 2: The Studio. It presents a further selection from the Future Architecture platform call for ideas, and focuses firmly on the nitty-gritty of practice with projects and strategies that are on-site or site ready to shake up that future. These are the inspirational solutions and ideas, which could soon be transforming the landscape of architecture and our cities, reasserting the agency of what architecture in its widest sense can offer and mean. Contributors include: Aleksandra Zarek; Andrej Strehovec; Plan Común; Esen Gökçe Özdamar and Murat Ateş; Guerilla Architects; Ignacio Gias; Jack Self; Jan Glasmeier, a.gor.a architects; Jana Čulek; Lavinia Scaletti; Léopold Lambert; Linnea Våglund and Leo Fidjeland; Manon Mollard; Urbz; Natasha Reid; Sara Neves and Felipe Estrela."--cprovided by distributor  aCC BY-NC-ND10aArchitectural criticism.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8500658310aCity planning.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8502628210aHousing.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8506260310aSpace (Architecture)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh8512590717aArchitectural criticism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst008131790http://id.worldcat.org/fast/81317917aArchitectural Space.2fast0(OCoLC)fst0112760117aHousing.2fast0(OCoLC)fst009622450http://id.worldcat.org/fast/96224517aUrbanism.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00862177 7aDiscursive works.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026089 7aEssay Collection.2fast0(OCoLC)fst014240321 aBatzenschlager, Thomas,econtributor.1 aCourrèges, Kim,econtributor.1 aČulek, Jana,econtributor.1 aEchanove, Matias,econtributor.1 aEstrela, Filipe,econtributor.1 aFerrari, Felipe de,econtributor.1 aFidjeland, Leo,econtributor.1 aGias, Ignacio,econtributor.1 aGiovanazzi, Lena,econtributor.1 aGlasmeier, Jan,econtributor.1 aGrass, Diego,econtributor.1 aHeilmeyer, Florian,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20092047471 aKafka, George,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20220062431 aLambert, Léopold,econtributor.1 aLovell, Sophie,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20043145081 aMollard, Manon,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/nb20190153791 aNeves, Sara,econtributor.1 aPortela, Diana,econtributor.1 aReid, Natasha,econtributor.1 aScaletti, Lavinia,econtributor.1 aSelf, Jack,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n20140515501 aShipwright, Fiona,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20200453971 aSiniloo, Janar,econtributor.1 aSrivastava, Rahul,econtributor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n892681981 aStrehovec, Andrej,econtributor.1 aVåglund, Linnea,econtributor.1 aWilson, Rob,eeditor.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20101898481 aZarek, Aleksandra,econtributor.2 a&beyond,eEditor.2 aGuerilla Architects,eContributor.2 aLibrary Stack,edistributor.40zAvailable to Stanford-affiliated users.uhttps:/